IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: sections 76 and 76A -- the nouns the part sga2 needs beyond the keel's core.
-- Nouns only: DECLARE and constants. No rule is written here. Every name begins with the label of the provision it belongs to
-- (s 76(2) ..., s 76A(5) ...), so that no other part can define the same name.
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact, or does answering it need the Act?

§ `Section 76: what the subsections name`

-- s 76(2): the means by which financial assistance may be given. The list is introduced by "includes" and ends "or otherwise".
DECLARE `s 76(2) means of giving financial assistance` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(2) the making of a loan`
    `s 76(2) the giving of a guarantee`
    `s 76(2) the provision of security`
    `s 76(2) the release of an obligation`
    `s 76(2) the release of a debt`
    `s 76(2) some other means`

-- s 76(16): the ways of acquiring shares or units of shares: "whether by way of purchase, subscription or otherwise".
DECLARE `s 76(16) way of acquiring` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(16) purchase`
    `s 76(16) subscription`
    `s 76(16) some other way`

-- The acts of a company that the prohibitions of s 76 name (the actions of the regulative rules of s 76).
DECLARE `s 76 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(1) give financial assistance for the purpose of, or in connection with, the acquisition or proposed acquisition of shares or units of shares`
    `s 76(1A)(a)(i) acquire shares or units of shares in the company`
    `s 76(1A)(a)(ii) purport to acquire shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company`
    `s 76(1A)(b)(i) lend money on the security of shares or units of shares in the company`
    `s 76(1A)(b)(ii) lend money on the security of shares or units of shares in a holding company or ultimate holding company of the company`
    `s 76(9C) give financial assistance under subsection (9A) or (9B) after a director has ceased to be satisfied or no longer has reasonable grounds`
    `s 76(9CA) give financial assistance under subsection (9BA) after a director has ceased to be satisfied that the terms are fair and reasonable`
    `s 76(14) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the order of the Court`
    `s 76(5) be an officer of the company who is in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)`

-- The penalty an offence of s 76 or s 76A carries: a fine and an imprisonment, and whether the Court may impose both.
DECLARE `s 76 penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine for the offence, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment for the offence, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the Court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment on the offender` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Section 76(12) and (13): who may oppose, and what the Court may do`

-- s 76(12): the persons who may apply to the Court opposing the giving of the financial assistance.
DECLARE `s 76(12) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(12)(a) a member of the company`
    `s 76(12)(b) a trustee for debenture holders of the company`
    `s 76(12)(c) a debenture holder of the company`
    `s 76(12)(d) a creditor of the company`
    `s 76(12)(e)(i) a member of the listed corporation or ultimate holding company that passed a special resolution mentioned in subsection (10)(b)`
    `s 76(12)(e)(ii) a trustee for debenture holders of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company`
    `s 76(12)(e)(iii) a debenture holder of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company`
    `s 76(12)(e)(iv) a creditor of that listed corporation or ultimate holding company`
    `s 76(12)(f) the Registrar`
    `s 76(12) some other person`

-- s 76(13)(b): what the Court may do on an application opposing the giving of the assistance.
DECLARE `s 76(13) order of the Court` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(13)(b)(iii) an order for the purchase by the company of the interests of dissentient members and the reduction accordingly of the capital of the company`
    `s 76(13)(b)(iv) an adjournment of the proceedings so that an arrangement may be made for the purchase, otherwise than by the company or a subsidiary of it, of the interests of dissentient members`
    `s 76(13)(b)(v) ancillary or consequential directions or orders`
    `s 76(13)(b)(vi) an order disapproving the giving of the financial assistance`
    `s 76(13)(b)(vi) an order approving the giving of the financial assistance`
    `s 76(13) some other order`

§ `Section 76A: the consequences`

-- s 76A(1): the contracts or transactions the subsection avoids.
DECLARE `s 76A(1) kind of contract or transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 76A(1)(a) a contract or transaction by which a company acquires or purports to acquire its own shares or units of its own shares, or shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company`
    `s 76A(1)(b) a contract or transaction by which a company lends money on the security of its own shares or units of its own shares, or of shares or units of shares in its holding company or ultimate holding company`
    `s 76A(1) some other contract or transaction`

-- s 76A(3): the persons the Court may authorise to give notice in the name of the company.
DECLARE `s 76A(3) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 76A(3) a member of the company`
    `s 76A(3) a holder of debentures of the company`
    `s 76A(3) a trustee for the holders of debentures of the company`
    `s 76A(3) a director of the company`
    `s 76A(3) some other person`

-- s 76A(5): the orders the Court may make under s 76A(4). The list is introduced by "include".
DECLARE `s 76A(5) order of the Court` IS ONE OF
    `s 76A(5)(a) an order directing a person to refund money or return property to the company or to another person`
    `s 76A(5)(b) an order directing a person to pay to the company or to another person a specified amount of the loss or damage suffered`
    `s 76A(5)(c) an order directing a person to indemnify the company or another person against loss or damage that may be suffered as a result of the contract or transaction or of its being or having become void`
    `s 76A(5) some other order`

-- The acts the offence of s 76A(11) names (the action of its regulative rule).
DECLARE `s 76A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76A(11) sign a certificate that the requirements of section 76(9A), (9B), (9BA) or (10) have been complied with, when any of them had not`
